    "notes": "Official Strat-O-Matic correction: Strat-O-Matic redid Wilson Ramos's 2010 advanced side and posted this corrected card image (992x560 scan, sourceImage) on its 'Baseball 2010 Corrections' announcement (sourceUrl). Read twice: (1) from the full scan, (2) from 3x-upscaled per-column crops; no differences. Markers: downTriangle ▼, upTriangle △ (each △ cell prints its default on the roll line and an italic 'SI* / lo (ss)' d20 split on the two lines directly beneath, before the next roll's line, so the binding is unambiguous: default in outcomes with range null, alternate ranged), '?' as questionMark, underlined class letters as 'underline:C'. 'plus injury' prints on its own line under HBP (LHP col3 roll11, RHP col1 roll3). A tiny-sample card: Ramos had 79 AB in 2010 (Minnesota and Washington), hence the run of DOUBLE results vs LHP. Validator CHECK (kept, genuine card limitation of a 79-AB sample): BA error .0162 vs the .015 bar (implied .267, actual .278; H/PA .253 vs .268) and BB .0153 (implied .040 vs actual .024). The card prints no WALK at all, so every implied walk comes from the average pitcher card, below which a 2-walk season cannot go; HR, 2B and SO fit within .006."
